<%--
Stat_Group - dashboard telemetry: a responsive grid of KPI stat tiles

default content - <Kpi_Cell> cells (the app's one KPI cell)

The dashboard is the one legitimate home for a headline stat strip (an entity
view keeps its telemetry in the sidebar - see Sidebar_Kpi_Group). Stat_Group
lays the same KPI cell out edge-to-edge across the top of an overview page:
four-up on a wide desktop, collapsing to two-up then one-up as the page
narrows. The cell is levered, not duplicated - a stat tile and a sidebar KPI
are the same display shape (uppercase label + large value + optional $alert),
so both render through Kpi_Cell; only the group layout differs.

Usage:
    <Stat_Group>
        <Kpi_Cell $tooltip="Projects in progress">
            <Slot:label>Active Projects</Slot:label>
            <Slot:value><%= _stats.active_projects %></Slot:value>
        </Kpi_Cell>
        <Kpi_Cell $alert=_has_overdue>
            <Slot:label>Overdue Tasks</Slot:label>
            <Slot:value><%= _stats.overdue_tasks %></Slot:value>
        </Kpi_Cell>
    </Stat_Group>
--%>
<Define:Stat_Group>
    <%= content() %>
</Define:Stat_Group>
